IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `voca-dates`

-- Motor Accident Insurance Act 1994 (Qld), s 37(2)-(3) and the s 4 definition of "motor vehicle accident" only,
-- brought in for the Victims of Crime Assistance Act 2009, s 36D(3): a victim assistance decision is deferred until a
-- motor accident claim is made and finally dealt with, unless the claim "is barred under the Motor Accident Insurance
-- Act 1994, section 37(3)" (or a late notice under s 37(3) was tried without success) and the applicant has a
-- reasonable excuse for not claiming "within the period mentioned in section 37(2)".
--
-- SEAT-NEUTRAL. The actor is the MAI Act's "claimant". The VOCA applicant's questions are in voca-seat.l4.
--
-- Edition: Motor Accident Insurance Act 1994 (act-1994-009), current in-force version on 22 September 2026, as
-- deposited at ../../../motor-accident-insurance-act-1994/registers/source-bundle/act-1994-009.txt. Nothing else in the
-- MAI Act is encoded: not the rest of s 37 (contents of the notice), not s 37A, not the limitation period for court
-- proceedings, not the insurer's duties.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Motor Accident Insurance Act 1994, s 37(2)-(3) -- notice of a motor accident claim`

-- s 4: "motor vehicle accident means an incident from which a liability for personal injury arises that is covered by
-- insurance under the statutory insurance scheme." The statutory insurance scheme (compulsory third-party (CTP)
-- insurance, with the Nominal Defendant for uninsured and unidentified vehicles) is a borrowed term, asked as a fact.
GIVEN `a liability for personal injury arose from the incident` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the liability is covered by insurance under the statutory insurance scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the incident is a motor vehicle accident (MAI s 4)` `a liability for personal injury arose from the incident` `the liability is covered by insurance under the statutory insurance scheme` IF
        `a liability for personal injury arose from the incident`
    AND `the liability is covered by insurance under the statutory insurance scheme`

-- The facts that fix the s 37(2) period.
DECLARE `Motor accident notice facts` HAS
    `the day of the accident`                                    IS A DATE
    `the motor vehicle can be identified`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `symptoms of the injury were immediately apparent`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day symptoms of the injury first appeared`              IS A DATE
    `the claimant has consulted a lawyer about a possible claim` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day the claimant first consulted a lawyer about it`     IS A DATE

-- s 37(2): "The notice must be given-- (a) if it is to be given to the Nominal Defendant because the motor vehicle can
-- not be identified--within 3 months after the motor vehicle accident; or (b) in any other case--within the period
-- ending on the earlier of the following dates-- (i) 9 months after the motor vehicle accident or, if symptoms of the
-- injury are not immediately apparent, the first appearance of symptoms of the injury; (ii) 1 month after the claimant
-- first consults a lawyer about the possibility of making a claim."
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Motor accident notice facts`
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the MAI s 37(2) period` `the facts` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the facts`'s `the motor vehicle can be identified`)
    THEN `the day that is` 3 `months after` (`the facts`'s `the day of the accident`)
    ELSE IF `the facts`'s `the claimant has consulted a lawyer about a possible claim`
         THEN IF `nine months` `is on or before` `one month after the lawyer`
              THEN `nine months`
              ELSE `one month after the lawyer`
         ELSE `nine months`
    WHERE
        `nine months` MEANS
            IF `the facts`'s `symptoms of the injury were immediately apparent`
            THEN `the day that is` 9 `months after` (`the facts`'s `the day of the accident`)
            ELSE `the day that is` 9 `months after` (`the facts`'s `the day symptoms of the injury first appeared`)
        `one month after the lawyer` MEANS `the day that is` 1 `months after` (`the facts`'s `the day the claimant first consulted a lawyer about it`)

-- s 37(3): "If notice of a claim is not given within the time fixed by this section, the obligation to give the notice
-- continues and a reasonable excuse for the delay must be given in the notice or by separate notice to the insurer but,
-- if a motor vehicle can not be identified and the notice is not given to the Nominal Defendant within 9 months after
-- the motor vehicle accident, the claim against the Nominal Defendant is barred."
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Motor accident notice facts`
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day before a claim against the Nominal Defendant is barred` `the facts` MEANS
    `the day that is` 9 `months after` (`the facts`'s `the day of the accident`)

-- Barred on a day: the vehicle cannot be identified, the 9 months have passed on that day, and notice was not given
-- within them.
GIVEN `the facts`                    IS A `Motor accident notice facts`
      `notice has been given`        IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day notice was given`     IS A DATE
      `the day asked about`          IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claim is barred under MAI s 37(3)` `the facts` `notice has been given` `the day notice was given` `the day asked about` IF
        NOT (`the facts`'s `the motor vehicle can be identified`)
    AND DATE_SERIAL `the day asked about` GREATER THAN DATE_SERIAL (`the last day before a claim against the Nominal Defendant is barred` `the facts`)
    AND NOT (    `notice has been given`
             AND `the day notice was given` `is on or before` (`the last day before a claim against the Nominal Defendant is barred` `the facts`))

DECLARE `Motor accident notice answer` IS ONE OF
    `notice of the claim is due by` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `notice was given within the s 37(2) period`
    `notice is late: it must still be given, with a reasonable excuse for the delay (MAI s 37(3))` HAS `the period ended on` IS A DATE
    `the claim against the Nominal Defendant is barred: no notice within 9 months after the accident (MAI s 37(3))` HAS `the 9 months ended on` IS A DATE

GIVEN `the facts`                    IS A `Motor accident notice facts`
      `notice has been given`        IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day notice was given`     IS A DATE
      `the day asked about`          IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Motor accident notice answer`
`the MAI s 37 answer for` `the facts` `notice has been given` `the day notice was given` `the day asked about` MEANS
    IF `the claim is barred under MAI s 37(3)` `the facts` `notice has been given` `the day notice was given` `the day asked about`
    THEN `the claim against the Nominal Defendant is barred: no notice within 9 months after the accident (MAI s 37(3))` (`the last day before a claim against the Nominal Defendant is barred` `the facts`)
    ELSE IF `notice has been given`
         THEN IF `the day notice was given` `is on or before` (`the last day of the MAI s 37(2) period` `the facts`)
              THEN `notice was given within the s 37(2) period`
              ELSE `notice is late: it must still be given, with a reasonable excuse for the delay (MAI s 37(3))` (`the last day of the MAI s 37(2) period` `the facts`)
         ELSE IF `the day asked about` `is on or before` (`the last day of the MAI s 37(2) period` `the facts`)
              THEN `notice of the claim is due by` (`the last day of the MAI s 37(2) period` `the facts`)
              ELSE `notice is late: it must still be given, with a reasonable excuse for the delay (MAI s 37(3))` (`the last day of the MAI s 37(2) period` `the facts`)

§§ `Regulative rule -- the claimant's notice`

-- Clock: days from the day of the accident (day 0).
DECLARE `MAI party` IS ONE OF `the claimant`

DECLARE `MAI act` IS ONE OF
    `give notice of the claim`
    `give notice of the claim, with a reasonable excuse for the delay`

-- s 37(2)-(3). Within the s 37(2) period, notice is owed. After it, "the obligation to give the notice continues" with a
-- reasonable excuse; for a vehicle that cannot be identified it ends in a bar at 9 months after the accident. The stable
-- l4 starts the LEST rule when it reads the first event or WAITUNTIL after the deadline, so the cases WAITUNTIL the day
-- after the s 37(2) period, and the rule's second window is counted from that day: 9 months less the period less 1.
-- For an identified vehicle s 37(3) sets no end, and the rule waits indefinitely.
GIVEN `days in the s 37(2) period`                IS A NUMBER
      `the vehicle can be identified`             IS A BOOLEAN
      `days from the day after the period to the end of the 9 months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `MAI party` `MAI act`
DECIDE `MAI s 37(2)-(3) -- the claimant must give notice of the claim within the period, and after it with a reasonable excuse` IS
    PARTY `the claimant`
    MUST  `give notice of the claim`
    WITHIN `days in the s 37(2) period`
    LEST  `the continuing obligation`
    WHERE
        `the continuing obligation` MEANS
            IF `the vehicle can be identified`
            THEN PARTY `the claimant`
                 MUST  `give notice of the claim, with a reasonable excuse for the delay`
            ELSE PARTY `the claimant`
                 MUST  `give notice of the claim, with a reasonable excuse for the delay`
                 WITHIN `days from the day after the period to the end of the 9 months`
                 LEST  BREACH BY `the claimant` BECAUSE "MAI s 37(3): notice was not given to the Nominal Defendant within 9 months after the motor vehicle accident, so the claim against the Nominal Defendant is barred"

-- The rule's numbers from the facts (day 0 is the day of the accident).
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Motor accident notice facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days in the MAI s 37(2) period for` `the facts` MEANS
    `the number of days from` (`the facts`'s `the day of the accident`) `to` (`the last day of the MAI s 37(2) period` `the facts`)

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Motor accident notice facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days after the MAI s 37(2) period to the bar for` `the facts` MEANS
    `days to the bar` MINUS `days in the period` MINUS 1
    WHERE
        `days to the bar` MEANS `the number of days from` (`the facts`'s `the day of the accident`) `to` (`the last day before a claim against the Nominal Defendant is barred` `the facts`)
        `days in the period` MEANS `the days in the MAI s 37(2) period for` `the facts`
